Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le07ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le07ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le07ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le07ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Hello?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> Is this Sally?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Yes ...\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> This is Maria. I'm Vanessa's coworker. She told me that I should get you to give me some advice.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Sure, what can I do for you?"}, {"time": "15000", "image": "engenn9le07ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> I live with two other people. I have problems getting my roommates to do chores around the house.  I do all the work. Don't you think it's a bit unfair?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> It's definitely not fair. Wouldn't you agree that you need to divide all the chores equally between the three of you?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> Yes, you're right. I want to do that, but I am scared to ask them. Is there an easier way?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Yes. Make a chore wheel. It's a great way to have your roommates participate in the chores. That would help, don't you think?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> That's a wonderful idea! My friend put one together at college and it was very effective."}, {"time": "53000", "image": "engenn9le07ob01re2img05.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Isn't it time you took a break and let your roommates help you?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> Yes, I'm so tired of doing all the laundry and cleaning up in the house. There are other chores like mowing the lawn, and dusting that also need to get done.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Wow!  First off you need to have them do their own laundry. Perhaps you could get a teenager in the neighborhood to mow the lawn. The dusting you can share. Don't you feel better now that you can have your friends' help?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Maria:</span> Yes, I do. Thanks Sally for everything!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Anytime."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sharing the Housework"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Chore Wheel"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le07ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Causative - <span class=\"italic\">get</span>/<span class=\"italic\">have</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use a causative verb when you want to talk about something that someone else did for you or for another person. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"italic\">get</span>/<span class=\"italic\">have </span>when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I have problems getting my roommates to do chores around the house."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's a great way to have your roommates participate in the chores. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She told me that I should get you to give me some advice. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "First off you need to have them do their own laundry. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Perhaps you could get a teenager in the neighborhood to mow the lawn."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br /><span class=\"italic\">Perhaps <span class=\"strong\">you </span>could <span class=\"strong\">get</span> a teenager in the neighborhood <span class=\"strong\">to mow</span> the lawn. </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this sentence <span class=\"italic\">you </span>pays/asks or persuades a <span class=\"italic\">teenager </span>to mow the lawn.</span> <br />"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the causative is: <br /><br /> Subject + <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + object + verb <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">You</span> need to <span class=\"strong\">have them do</span> their own laundry.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "or"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">get</span> + object + infinitive  <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">You get your roommates to participate</span> in chores.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Negative Questions To Encourage Agreement"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Negative questions have a different meaning than regular questions. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A negative question can be used to ask for confirmation of something you believe to be true."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Wouldn't you agree that you need to divide all the chores equally between the three of you? "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Isn't it time you took a break and let your roommates help you?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "That would help, don't you think?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't you feel better now that you can have your friends' help?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul> \t<li> \t<span class=\"italic\">Don't you think it's a bit unfair?</span> \t\t <ul> \t\t\t<li>(= <span class=\"italic\">I think it's a bit unfair.</span>)</li> \t\t</ul> \t</li> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With this type of question, you anticipate that the listener will agree with you and answer 'yes'.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you can add the question at the end of the statement. This is more casual."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br /><span class=\"italic\">That would help, don't you think?</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about doing household chores."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to dust"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to wipe the dust "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are other chores like mowing the lawn, and dusting that also need to get done.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to clean up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the process of cleaning or organizing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm so tired of doing all the laundry and cleaning up in the house."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mow the lawn"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cut the grass"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are other chores like mowing the lawn."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chore "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "work around a house"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Wouldn't you agree that you need to divide all the chores equally between the three of you? "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "effective "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "able to accomplish a purpose"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My friend put chore wheel together at college and it was very effective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "laundry "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "wash the clothes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm so tired of doing all the laundry and cleaning up in the house. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put together"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to make"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My friend put a chore wheel together at college and it was very effective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le07ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "For fun, make a chore wheel for the people in your family or for you and friends."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out online how to make the chore wheel. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make one up dividing up household chores, if it's for your family."}, {"type": "text", "content": " If it's for friends, pretend you are all living together in a house and sharing household tasks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Don't forget to be fair when you divide everything up!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bring your wheel to class and show a partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss why you divided the tasks the way you did."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find out how to make a chore wheel."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use vocabulary for domestic activities on it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss why I divided the chores that way with a partner."}]}]}